<http://data.silknow.org/object/c95307c4-63f1-3267-ba89-8545a4d5f992>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Roses, thistles and eglantines, butterflies, birds and caterpillars decorate this skillfully embroidered gentleman’s nightcap. Despite its name, this type of cap would also have functioned as an informal, indoor article of clothing during the daylight hours."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/96b69432-2409-3858-bb01-25d8dbedda25> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e3094cd0-300c-3432-806a-c02c164cba44> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e25c3690-363a-3a1f-bb70-e3131a0a2a9e> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/88500e58-b9f7-3452-97af-9ebaeba7fccf> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Roses, thistles and eglantines, butterflies, birds and caterpillars decorate this skillfully embroidered gentleman’s nightcap. Despite its name, this type of cap would also have functioned as an informal, indoor article of clothing during the daylight hours."@en ;
